// test-error
// test-adr: 057
// Issue #1724 in the operand typer (#1668's merge of main). A declaration's
// written type is qualified by ADR-057 against the scope types ITS file can
// see. In motor-mode-bad.cnx, a bare `Mode` inside the reopened scope Motor is
// the global enum, because motor-mode-decl.cnx's `Motor.Mode` is in this run
// but not in that file's include closure. So `Mode bad <- global.Speed.HIGH`
// is E0428.
//
// Qualified against every file in the run, `Mode` became `Motor__Mode`, which
// that file does not see declared: the written type went untyped, and the
// enum-safety check was skipped. The E0428 vanished, a silent false negative.
// The `ok` declaration is the control, which must stay silent.
#include "modes.cnx"
#include "motor-mode-decl.cnx"
#include "motor-mode-bad.cnx"

i32 main() {
    return 0;
}
